## Feature: Button Group
Priority: High
Status: Pending

### Overview
A wrapper component that groups multiple Button children into a single visual unit. Supports horizontal and vertical layout, seamless styling (first/middle/last radius and border collapse), and group-level isDisabled to disable all buttons inside.

### Requirements

#### 1. Basic Button Group
- Render a container with `role="group"`
- Accept `Button` components (or compatible elements) as children
- Apply base BEM class: `.aceui-button-group`
- Support `orientation` prop: `'horizontal'` (default) | `'vertical'`
- Horizontal: `display: inline-flex`, `flex-direction: row`, no gap so buttons touch
- Vertical: `flex-direction: column`, no gap so buttons touch

#### 2. Seamless Strip Styling
- Override radius of direct Button children so the group looks like one rounded rectangle
- First child (horizontal): round left only; inner edge (right) 0
- Last child (horizontal): round right only; inner edge (left) 0
- Middle children: `border-radius: 0`
- Vertical: first child round top only; last child round bottom only; middle 0
- Use direct-child selectors: `.aceui-button-group > .aceui-button`

#### 3. Border Collapse (Bordered Variant)
- For bordered Buttons inside the group, collapse inner borders so no double lines between buttons
- Use design token `--aceui-button-bordered-border-width` (defined in design-tokens.css)
- Remove or overlap inner border between adjacent buttons (e.g. negative margin or border-right: 0 on all but last)

#### 4. Group Disabled
- Support `isDisabled` prop (boolean)
- When `isDisabled={true}`, disable all buttons inside: clone children and pass `isDisabled={true}` to each child that accepts it
- For non-Button children, wrap or apply `aria-disabled="true"` and `pointer-events: none` as fallback

#### 5. Props and Accessibility
- Props: `children`, `isDisabled`, `orientation`, `className`, `testId`, `ariaLabel`
- Container: `role="group"`, `aria-label={ariaLabel}` when provided
- Export `ButtonGroupProps` interface

#### 6. Design Tokens
- Reuse radius tokens (`--aceui-radius-small`, `--aceui-radius-medium`, etc.) for first/last child overrides
- Reuse border width tokens for collapse styling

### Out of Scope (Phase 2)
- Split button (primary action + dropdown in one bar) — deferred until Dropdown/Menu primitive exists

---